Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:04.47,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\fad(160,160)}如果7月31日是你的生日,这段\N故事送给你。
Dialogue: 1,0:00:00.00,0:00:04.47,EN,,0,0,0,,{\fad(160,160)}A birthday story for July 31.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.04,0:00:11.81,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\fad(160,160)}1965年的今天,JK罗林出生\N,他从小就想成为作家。
Dialogue: 1,0:00:05.04,0:00:11.81,EN,,0,0,0,,{\fad(160,160)}Born in 1965, J.K. Rowling dreamed of writ\Ning.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.48,0:00:20.29,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\fad(160,160)}1990年,一般严悟的火车上,\N一个戴眼镜的男孩,突然出现在他
Dialogue: 1,0:00:12.48,0:00:20.29,EN,,0,0,0,,{\fad(160,160)}On a delayed train, a boy with glasses app\Neared in her mind.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.06,0:00:27.53,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\fad(160,160)}他花了五年完成第一本故事,投稿\N后,也曾被许多出版社拒绝。
Dialogue: 1,0:00:21.06,0:00:27.53,EN,,0,0,0,,{\fad(160,160)}Rejections did not stop her.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.14,0:00:33.53,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\fad(160,160)}直到1997年,哈利波特,神秘\N的魔法时,出版。
Dialogue: 1,0:00:28.14,0:00:33.53,EN,,0,0,0,,{\fad(160,160)}In 1997, Harry Potter found its first read\Ners.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.32,0:00:39.09,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\fad(160,160)}那个只存在脑海里的世界,开始走\N进全球读者的生命。
Dialogue: 1,0:00:34.32,0:00:39.09,EN,,0,0,0,,{\fad(160,160)}Her story reached readers around the world\N.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:39.80,0:00:44.41,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\fad(160,160)}他留下的不只是魔法世界,而是一\N个提醒。
Dialogue: 1,0:00:39.80,0:00:44.41,EN,,0,0,0,,{\fad(160,160)}Imagination can change a life.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.08,0:00:48.35,ZH,,0,0,0,,{\fad(160,160)}有些故事,要先有人愿意相信他。
Dialogue: 1,0:00:45.08,0:00:48.35,EN,,0,0,0,,{\fad(160,160)}Some stories begin when someone believes.